.TH "MEDIAKEYSESSION.MESSAGE_EVENT" "3JS" "October 27, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
MediaKeySession.message_event \- MediaKeySession: message event
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Secure context:\f[R] This feature is available only in secure
contexts (HTTPS).
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]message\f[B]\f[R] event of the \f[CR]MediaKeySession\f[R]
interface fires when a message is generated by the content decryption
module.
.SH SYNTAX
Use the event name in \f[CR]addEventListener()\f[R]:
.IP
.EX
addEventListener(\(dqmessage\(dq, (event) => { })
.EE
.PP
Alternatively, assign to the event handler property of the interface:
.IP
.EX
onmessage = (event) => { }
.EE
.SH EVENT TYPE
A \f[CR]MediaKeyMessageEvent\f[R].
Inherits from \f[CR]Event\f[R].
